sbase (since 3de61ef, 2024-12-19, "rev, tail: replace hardcoded code by
UTF8_POINT macro"): the test was `(c & 0xC0) == 0x80`, "is a UTF-8
continuation byte", and UTF8_POINT(c) is the opposite -- "starts a code
point". So rev printed every line unreversed, and tail -m counted
continuation bytes instead of characters. Negated back.

